# A Decimal keeps the places its column says, and a Fraction keeps everything.
#
# `Decimal(2)` is money: two places, held exactly. A product or a quotient is
# worked out exactly and rounded once, half away from zero, to the places its
# type has: a Decimal beside a finer one takes the finer, and a quotient takes
# ten places or the finer of its sides. A bare `Decimal` keeps ten.
#
# A Fraction is the exact rational. `1/3 * 3` is 0.9999999999 in decimals and
# `<1/3> * 3` is 1 in fractions. And what a column that declares nothing cannot
# hold in a Decimal it holds as a Fraction: 10**100 is not an error.

sheet Prices

Price : Decimal(2)
Rate  : Decimal(4)

| Item   | Price | Qty | Rate   | Net | Tax | Share | Running |
| ------ | ----- | --- | ------ | --- | --- | ----- | ------- |
| Pen    | 1.20  | 10  | 0.0725 | *   | *   | *     | *       |
| Book   | 19.99 | 2   | 0.0725 | *   | *   | *     | *       |
| Lamp   | 34.50 | 1   | 0.0825 | *   | *   | *     | *       |
| Cable  | 7.05  | 4   | 0.0825 | *   | *   | *     | *       |

Net     := Price * Qty
Tax     := Price * Rate
Share   := Price / Prices.Price.sum()
Running := Price.cum_sum()

sheet Thirds

| N | Decimal | Fraction | Back | Exact |
| - | ------- | -------- | ---- | ----- |
| 3 | *       | *        | *    | *     |
| 7 | *       | *        | *    | *     |
| 9 | *       | *        | *    | *     |

Decimal  := 1 / N
Fraction := <1> / N
Back     := Decimal * N
Exact    := Fraction * N

sheet Googol

| Power | Big | Tiny | Product |
| ----- | --- | ---- | ------- |
| 50    | *   | *    | *       |
| 100   | *   | *    | *       |

Big     := 10 ** Power
Tiny    := <1> / Big
Product := Big * Tiny
